# std.function: function types, their `Fn` bound and the `Tuple` marker trait
# (spec/lang/07-functions.md#function-type-constructors).
#
# In a type position, `Fn[I, O, $R]` and `SuspendFn[I, O, $R]` are the
# constructors that `fn(...) -> O $ R` and `fn!(...) -> O $ R` stand for.
# In a bound, `Fn[I, O, $R]` is the trait below. The compiler supplies its
# implementation for every matching plain function type.

# An empty sealed marker trait that every tuple type implements: `()`,
# `(A,)`, and a tuple with a rest element included
# (r-fn.type.ctor.tuple-trait, r-fn.type.ctor.tuple-trait.rest). Only the
# compiler implements it, as it does `Inspectable` (r-trait.sealed.tuple).
## The empty sealed marker trait that every tuple type implements, `()` and `(A,)` included.
## See [fn.type.ctor.tuple-trait](../../spec/lang/07-functions.md#r-fn.type.ctor.tuple-trait).
pub trait Tuple

## The static-dispatch trait implemented by every plain function value.
## See [fn.trait.decl](../../spec/lang/07-functions.md#r-fn.trait.decl).
pub trait Fn[I < Tuple, O, $ R = $ ()]:
    ## Calls this function with the parameter tuple `args`.
    @intrinsic("fn_call")
    fn call(&self, args: I) -> O $ R
